{
  "title": "Fireball spawns its zone, locks the creatures inside, applies saves, and discards everything",
  "source": "A Fireball card with a circle zone",
  "description": "Aldric (spell_dc 14) spawns a Fireball card whose zone (circle, radius 4) is copied with it and remapped, drags the zone onto the map over goblin1 and goblin2 but not goblin3, and locks one save row per target. The zone is nudged (targets change, rows do not). 8d6 rolls 27; goblin1 (dex +2) rolls 13 and passes for floor(27/2) = 13, goblin2 (dex +0, 3 damage already) rolls 9 and fails for 27. Apply all is group 7. Lowering goblin1's dex_save to -5 drifts its row's live damage_dealt to 27 while group 7 still records 13. Discard removes the zone, the card, and both rows. Log groups: 0 spawn, 1 move zone, 2 Lock targets, 3 nudge zone, 4 Roll damage, 5-6 Roll save, 7 Apply all, 8 set dex_save, 9 Discard.",
  "setup": {
    "boards": [
      {
        "id": "map",
        "name": "Map"
      },
      {
        "id": "shelf",
        "name": "Binder shelf"
      }
    ],
    "characters": ["aldric", "goblin1", "goblin2", "goblin3"],
    "objects": [
      {
        "id": "aldric",
        "note": "The caster, at x=2 on the y=10 line, well outside every placement of the circle. Each creature is a character that owns itself, so it.owner is set (DESIGN §4.4: owner points at a character).",
